# NOTHING IN /docs IS IGNORED. Upstream's `/docs/*.md` rule used to live here,
# for GZDoom's own generated docs, and it caught OUR specifications instead --
# three times, each time silently, each time found only because someone went
# looking for a file's history and there was none.
#
#   1. The six GAME_*.md reference manuals the whole game port is written
#      against, plus the NATIVE_*.md rules. Rescued with !/docs/GAME_*.md and
#      !/docs/NATIVE_*.md.
#   2. REMAROTH_MEASURED.md, the authoritative record of everything checked
#      against the running original, and the SURF_* rules. Rescued the same way.
#   3. docs/TRIGGERS_the_use_key_problem.md, 2026-10-02. The commit named "The
#      trigger layer is unreachable from play, for three separate reasons" does
#      not contain it: `git show --stat` on 4155d44366 lists three sources and
#      three capture files and no document. Meanwhile the evening handoff had
#      elevated that page to "THE EXACT NEXT STEP" for the next lane -- so the
#      most-cited new document in the project had no history and a `git clean`
#      would have taken it.
#
# The exception list was the wrong shape: every rescue added the prefix that had
# just been lost, and the next new prefix was always missed. There was never
# anything to protect, either -- every .md in /docs is ours, and GZDoom's
# generated docs have never been checked in here at all. So the rule is gone
# rather than patched. If upstream docs ever do land in /docs, ignore them BY
# NAME.

